WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.811
Idea. Your pocket money rises from twenty dollars to twenty-five. That is five dollars more, compared with the twenty you started with. Five out of twenty is twenty-five per cent.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:21.327
So percentage change is new minus old, divided by old, times one hundred. Always divide by the old, earlier value.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:33.687
Inflation is measured with the consumer price index. If the base year index is one hundred and it is now one hundred and twelve, prices have risen twelve per cent since the base year.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:47.460
Method. Step one, pick the two values the question asks for. From 2021 to 2023, use four hundred and four hundred and sixty. Skip 2022.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:56.338
Step two, find the change: sixty. Step three, divide by the old value and times by one hundred: fifteen per cent.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:08.939
If the old index is not one hundred, use the full formula. From one hundred and twenty to one hundred and twenty-six is six, divided by one hundred and twenty: five per cent.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:19.567
A fall gives a minus sign. Fifty down to forty-five is minus ten per cent. Step five, round as asked, and always add the per cent sign.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:40.549
Worked example. Here is a real question from November 2021. The table shows a firm's profit from 2017 to 2019. Calculate the percentage change in profit between 2017 and 2019, to two decimal places. Two marks.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:54.185
The old value is 2017: eighty thousand seven hundred and fifty dollars. The new value is 2019: eighty-seven thousand one hundred dollars. Ignore 2018.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:14.097
The change is six thousand three hundred and fifty. Divide by eighty thousand seven hundred and fifty and times by one hundred: seven point eight six three. To two decimal places, seven point eight six per cent. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:23.242
Common mistake. A common mistake is dividing by the new value. That gives seven point two nine per cent, which is wrong.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:29.238
Another is using index minus one hundred when the old index is not one hundred.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:46.837
Your turn. Now you try. A country's C P I was one hundred and forty in 2023 and one hundred and forty-seven in 2024. Calculate the rate of inflation, to two decimal places. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:59.299
Answer. The change is seven. Seven divided by one hundred and forty, times one hundred, is five. To two decimal places, five point zero zero per cent.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.655
So the price level rose by five per cent of where it started.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:15.192
Remember: pick old and new, find the change, divide by the old value, times one hundred, then round and add the per cent sign. Now try the practice questions.
